From parkhurs at indiana.edu  Sat Aug  4 22:22:38 2001
From: parkhurs at indiana.edu (David Parkhurst)
Date: Sat, 04 Aug 2001 17:22:38 -0500
Subject: Summary: Controlling order of trellis conditioning factor
Message-ID: <004101c11d34$22bb4e10$aaa7550c@spea.indiana.edu>

I asked:  >I have a trellis plot with a formula like y ~ x | factor, where
the values
>of factor are text strings.  I want the panels to be plotted in the same
>order that the factor values are listed in the data frame, but trellis
>places them in alphabetical order.  How can I get them in original order?

Thanks to the 18 kind folks who suggested solutions.  I won't quote them all
here (one or two didn't work for me), but the one that solved my problem
(from Remy van de Ven) was:

A <- as.character(A)   # Where A is the factor
A <- factor(A, levels=unique(A))

It may be relevant that I originally created my dataframe using
read.table(), and had immediately executed
A <- as.factor(A) immediately thereafter.

Again, thanks to all.

Dave

