On Wed, 8 Aug 2001, Alexander Lawhead wrote:

> I've started using the rpart library to build regression trees for a
> prediction problem. Is there a way of forcing the rpart routine (or the
> vanilla CART routines in S-plus) to provide all splits for a given tree,
> for example:

Do you mean all *prunings* in the cost-complexity sequence?  If so, I think
the latest (unreleased as yet) rpart code does so for regression trees.

Similarly, tree() (there is no `vanilla CART routines in S-plus' and CART a
trademark) always did give the full cost-complexity sequence.

Note that for classification trees and misclassification costs, the full
cost-complexity sequence does not necessarily drop one split at a time, and
this happens frequently.  That is less likely with the pruning of
regression trees, but I believe can happen.

BTW, there is a phenomenal number of possible prunings: see the CART book
(Breiman et al, 1984).

