From: robert.platt at mcgill.ca (Robert Platt)
Date: Thu, 09 Aug 2001 12:46:55 -0400
Subject: Re: "Position" of a scalar in an ordered vector - Thanks!
References: <003101c120ec$4e5b9500$c452cac7@BioStats.mchri.mcgill.ca>
Message-ID: <006101c120f2$e61f4cf0$c452cac7@BioStats.mchri.mcgill.ca>

This list always amazes me.

I posted at 11:59 EST, and went to get lunch.  When I returned 
at 12:30, there were 9 solutions to my problem!

Thanks to Vadim Ogranovich, Eric Kostello, Bill Dunlap, Kevin
Brand, Steve McKinney, Jose Pinheiro, Hong Ooi, and Joseph
Verducci.

The solutions were all simple, and efficient.  Some one-line solutions
were:

seq(along=treatment.dates)[treatment.dates >= failure][1]

or

min(which(treatment.dates>=failure))

or

failVisit <- function(trt.dates, fail.date) sum(trt.dates < fail.date) + 1

Thanks again!

RP
