Message-ID: <Pine.GSO.4.31.0108100710050.3891-100000@auk.stats>

On Fri, 10 Aug 2001, Nick Ellis wrote:

> Hm. Very subtle. If you change the dummy argument of print.thang from thing
> to x, the function will work properly. I seem to remember somethang about
> generic functions having to have an argument name x. Can anyone elucidate?

Methods should have the same principal argument name as the generic (which
for print is `x').  If not, in S3, the principal argument gets evaluated
twice. See `S Programming' page 77.  Even more peculiar things can happen
in the latest versions of S-PLUS 6 (e.g. for Windows).

(I know that's terse, but the details are subtle and I don't want to
rewrite them here for fear of making a slip.)

