Subject: mediator in lme
Message-ID: <3B73A472.9ADDDCE5@psyres-stuttgart.de>

dear s-plus users,

via a hlm model (psychotherapy effectiveness study, longitudinal
unbalanced data: 1,2 or three measurement points), i examined whether
outcome over time is affected by a structural variable (waiting time).
the model is like this:

psych.lme <- lme (fixed = SCSW.010 ~ IN.THER * NANF.KOS, random = ~
IN.THER | CODE, data = diss.gr,  na.action="na.omit")
with: SCSW.010 = outcome (continuous, measured every time);
IN.THER = time in psychotherapy in days (continuous);
NANF.KOS = waiting time for start of psychotherapy in days (discrete
factor, 4 levels: long, rather long, rather short, short);
CODE = participant's code.

now, since i didn't find a direct effect of waiting time on outcome, i
would like to know whether this effect is mediated by another variable
(quality of patient-therapist relationship; continuous, measured every
time). my question is: how do i best measure such a mediating effect? a
first idea would be to "simply" assess all possible relations, including
interactions:

psych2.lme <- lme (fixed = SCSW.010 ~ IN.THER * NANF.KOS + IN.THER *
ABSW.001 + IN.THER * NANF.KOS * ABSW.001,  random = ~ IN.THER | CODE,
data = diss.gr, na.action="na.omit")
with absw.001 = quality of patient-therapist relationship.

... but i doubt that this is the right way. as always, i would be
extremely grateful for any suggestions from this great group.

thanks,
bernd puschner

