the resulting data frames together.

**************************************************

Jan Brogger wrote:

Couldn't you import the entire file using import.data, then dump the stuff 
you don't need ? Assuming the data file is too large, I think your best bet 
would be to convert the SPSS file to a text file (which can probably be 
done automatically in a script), then do one of the following
1) use scan() and list the columns you don't need. Scan is fast but if the 
file is large, this may not be feasible.
2) use a perl/grep/awk script or something to extract only the columns you 
need to a file. Then read this into S+.
Or
3) use a commerical data translation program (e.g. DBMS/COPY) to extract 
only the columns you need from either the SPSS or text file to another 
file. Then read this file into S+.

