Subject: RE: [S] Cronbach's alpha code?

Does anybody have or know the location of S-plus code for calculating
Cronbach's alpha? If not, do you know of a good reference for how to
calculate it that can be accessed digitally, so I can try to write the code
myself?

Thanks very much,
Sam Merrill
- ----------------------------------------------------------------------

You may have had a response to this already, but the link below was recently
posted on this list.

http://www.biostat.wustl.edu/s-news/s-news-archive/200008/msg00201.html

Also, in case it's useful, here is a somewhat clumsier approach in a
function that I wrote.

cralpha<-function(obsmat){

######################################################
# Function to calculate Cronbach's ALPHA from
# matrix of raw scores with no missing values
#
# Michael Thomas
# University of Southern California
# Rossier School of Education
#
# Based on Pedhazur 5.17 and
# Nunnally & Bernstein 6-26
#
# File Name: E:\SPLUS_fun\cralpha.fun
######################################################

######################################################
# Convert entered raw score matrix: obsmat
# to deviation scores
######################################################

Xd<-scale(obsmat, scale=FALSE, center=T)

######################################################
# Get SSCP for Xd
# denominator is n, not n-1 (Pedhazur, p. 96)
######################################################

Xd.cov<-crossprod(Xd) * (nrow(Xd)^-1)

######################################################
# Calculate alpha
# ncol(Xd) = number of items = k
######################################################

alpha<-
( ncol(Xd) / (ncol(Xd) - 1) ) *
(1 - (sum(diag(Xd.cov)) / sum(Xd.cov)))

######################################################
# Output value for Coefficient Alpha
######################################################

print("Coefficient Alpha:")
list(alpha=alpha)

}

