> The same phenomenon does not occur in Splus 3.4, that's all we have
> tested.

Take a closer look in the green book.  In S4 auto-printing is done by the
function show(), which is an S4-style generic, rather than print().  As
class "foo" is an S3-style class, that calls

> print(x)
foo

and that has cached the information about methods.  (Omit the central `x'
to see this.)

Remember that S-PLUS 5.x and 6 are based on what is effectively a
completely different engine from S-PLUS 3.4, one that tries to be
more efficient with large objects and calculations.  You have to treat
classes much more seriously now.

