Many thanks to Drs. Jose Pinheiro and Douglas Bates for solving my problem.
Dr. Pinheiro points out that the plot can be accomplished but not by using a
simple argument to the plot method. The nlsList object loses some attributes
in the subsetting  and code to restore the attributes is required before the
subset plots correctly. He suggests the following code:

> Wb4.int <- intervals(Wb4.lis)
> Wb4.grpName <- attr(Wb4.int, "groupsName")
> Wb4.int <- Wb4.int[-17,,]
> class(Wb4.int) <- "intervals.lmList"
> attr(Wb4.int, "groupsName") <- Wb4.grpName
> plot(Wb4.int)

The plot method yield an interval plot correctly excluding parameters of
Tree 17.

Thank again to Drs. Jose Pinheiro and Douglas Bates,

Richard

