show the predicted survival curves for the significant interactions (among 
factors) - i.e. an equivalent display of partial fits/least square means 
for survival analysis.  V&Rp377 has a bit of code that might be a start 
(translating a survReg fit to a plot(survfit()) call via event 
time*exp[-linear.predictor]; this is I assume the curve for an "average" 
individual given the covariates in the model), and Terry Therneau provided 
this type of strategy for an unweighted cox model:

 fit <- coxph(Surv(event,cens) ~ strata(cjdens) + jft*jfa, data=juv.work)
