> I would like to create a data frame by adding rows using rbind.  But I know
> it is rather inefficient to use rbind within for loops.  So, I am requesting
> the group how to use rbind by avoiding using it in nested for loops.

Just avoid rbind.  Set up a data frame of the final size (with
pCount*sCount rows here), and replace

               newDF <- rbind(newDF, out)
by
               newDF[j + (i-1)*sCount, ] <- out

Since append() does similar things (you could just use c() in your usage),
you may want to speed up quantros.quartersRow by pre-allocating space.
Also, are you sure you want to call date()?  That's when the code is run,
and the second instance is not even used.

