My thanks to Nick Ellis.

There are two ways to solve this problem.

First, put a <- menuDescribe(air) into the "Execute using [Execute] topic"
box, press the button (this creates a permanent object a in Splus) then type

a

into the Request box and press the button.

Second, create functions that turn off the invisibility

visible <- function(x = NULL)
{
        assign(".Auto.print", T, frame = sys.parent(2))
        x
}
echo.invisible <- function(x)
{
        y <- x
        visible(y)
}

then type echo.invisible(menuDescribe(air,print.p=F)) in the Request box.
(The print.p argument prevents you getting two copies printed.)

Try testing it with expressions like "invisible(1)" and
"echo.invisible(invisible(2))"

Brenda Yang

