Dear S group;

This is a terribly simple question but it's a little complex for me: I would 
like to subscript based on multiple values.

a<-c(1,2,3,NA,5)
a<-rbind(a,c(2,2,-1,3,3))
a<-rbind(a,c(3,3,3,3,3))
a<-rbind(a,c(2,2,2,2,2))
a<-rbind(a,c(999,999,999,1,1))

thus a = 1,2,3,NA,5
         2,2,-1,3,3
         3,3, 3,3,3
         2,2, 2,2,2
       999,999,999,1,1
how can I subscript in one command rows that do not contain either -1, greater 
than 999 or NA?  I would like to get this as a result:

a=3,3,3,3,3
  2,2,2,2,2
but I haven't been able to combine !<0, !>999 and !is.na successfully.

Ideas?

Thank you very much;

Phillip

