If the object "list" was a function object, then you can expect problems.
The S language has fairly laid-back scoping rules, and there are no special
protections for core functions like list, vector, c, etc.  Redefining any of
these is likely to cause problems, especially in GUI-based versions of
S-PLUS which use S for a lot of their internal workings.

In recent versions of S-PLUS at least, creating non-function objects with
such names shouldn't have serious consequences besides annoying warnings
here and there.

# David

