From anna at hsph.harvard.edu  Thu Aug 30 21:56:06 2001
From: anna at hsph.harvard.edu (Anna Legedza)
Date: Thu, 30 Aug 2001 17:56:06 -0400
Subject: first occurrence solutions
Message-ID: <200108302156.f7ULu6u17967@hsph.harvard.edu>

Dear Splus folks,

Thanks to the many people who replied to a request for help, including
Phil Spector, Samuel Buttrey, Remy van de Ven, Steve McKinney, Nick Ellis ,
Rolf Turner, James Holtman, Bert Gunter, Vince Carey, David Lorenz,
Jingshan Z., Kevin Brand, Chuck Taylor, and Chris Andrews.

Original post:
> I would like to extract those rows in temp
> > temp[1:9,]
>    V3 V5
>  1  1  1
>  2  1  1
>  3  1  1
>  4  2  1
>  5  0  0
>  6  1  0
>  7  0  0
>  8  1  1
>  9  1  1
> according to values in the column labelled "V3".
> Every time I get to the first in a
> sequence of identical values in "V3", I would like
> to extract that row to obtain the following
>    V3 V5
>  1  1  1
>  4  2  1
>  5  0  0
>  6  1  0
>  7  0  0
>  8  1  1
>

There seemed to be three different short flavors of doing it (listed
in no particular order). All involve prepending a dummy term to the vectpor
in order to ensure that the first observation is selected.

1. Using length():

   last <- c(-99,temp$V3[-length(temp$V3)])
   temp[temp$V3 != last,]

2. Using rle():

   > temp <-
   +   cbind(c(1, 1, 1, 2, 0, 1, 0, 1, 1),
   +         c(1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1))
   > temp
        [,1] [,2] 
        [1,]    1    1
        [2,]    1    1
        [3,]    1    1
        [4,]    2    1
        [5,]    0    0
        [6,]    1    0
        [7,]    0    0
        [8,]    1    1
        [9,]    1    1
        > 
        > 
        > indexes <- 1 + cumsum(rle(temp[, 1])$length)
        > indexes <- c(1, indexes[-length(indexes)])
        > indexes
        [1] 1 4 5 6 7 8
        > temp[indexes, ]
             [,1] [,2] 
             [1,]    1    1
             [2,]    2    1
             [3,]    0    0
             [4,]    1    0
             [5,]    0    0
             [6,]    1    1

3. Using diff():

   foo<-c(T,diff(temp$V3)!=0)
   new.frame<-temp[foo,]

Thank you very much,
Anna

